<%# Portfolio value over time.

    Three things were wrong in the markup rather than the design. The h2 carried **two** class
    attributes - `class="text-lg font-normal tracking-tight leading-none" class="tracking-tight"` -
    and a browser keeps the first and drops the second silently. It was also text-lg font-normal
    where design.md's section title is text-base font-semibold, so the one card with a heading had
    a heading unlike every other card. And the empty state was hand-built with a slate-400 icon
    (2.5:1) instead of the shared component.

    The 300px canvas height stays an inline style: Chart.js measures its container, and a Tailwind
    height class on the wrapper is what the arbitrary-value rule would otherwise force here. %>
<% chart_data = @portfolio.chart_data %>

<%= render layout: "components/ui/card",
           locals: { title: "Portfolio value over time",
                     subtitle: "Cash plus the value of everything you hold",
                     class: "h-full" } do %>
  <% if chart_data.length < 2 %>
    <%= render layout: "components/ui/empty_state",
               locals: { icon: "chart-line",
                         title: "Not enough data yet",
                         body: "Your chart appears once two months of value have been recorded." } do %>
    <% end %>
  <% else %>
    <div class="relative" style="height: 300px;">
      <canvas
        data-controller="portfolio-chart"
        data-portfolio-chart-data-value="<%= chart_data.to_json %>"></canvas>
    </div>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
